IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`
IMPORT `cdba-act`

-- Tests for the Canada Disability Benefit Act, with the working beside each assertion. The
-- assent dates below are illustrative inputs: the text shows none.

§ `Act s 4 -- tests`

-- An otherwise eligible person in August 2025 (born 10 May 1990, DTC-eligible, resident, a
-- citizen, no partner, no custody, no suspension), with the return either filed or not.
GIVEN filed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`a person in August 2025 whose return is` filed MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS YMD 2025 8 15
        `date of birth`                               IS YMD 1990 5 10
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS filed
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

`an allocation payment the person was entitled to, resting on the certificate` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS TRUE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS FALSE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS TRUE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS TRUE

-- Eligible for the allocation: eligible for a benefit.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` TRUE) FALSE EMPTY
-- Not eligible for the allocation (no return) and no certificate payment: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE) FALSE EMPTY
-- Not eligible for the allocation but eligible for the supplemental amount: eligible for a benefit.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE) TRUE (LIST `an allocation payment the person was entitled to, resting on the certificate`)
-- A certificate but no payment after it: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE) TRUE EMPTY

§ `Act s 5 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Act s 6 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the person must provide the Minister with the information` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the person must provide the Minister with the information` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person must provide the Minister with the information` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person must provide the Minister with the information` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person must provide the Minister with the information` FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `Act s 7 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Minister is authorized to collect and use the person's Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister is authorized to collect and use the person's Social Insurance Number` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister is authorized to collect and use the person's Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE

§ `Act s 8 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` `a department or agency of the Government of Canada` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` `a department or agency of the Government of Canada` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` `a department or agency of a province` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` `a department or agency of a province` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` `anyone else` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must make the agreement public` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must make the agreement public` FALSE

§ `Act s 9 -- tests`

#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `an operation of a law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` EQUALS `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `an assignment, charge, attachment or giving as security` EQUALS `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under an Act of Parliament other than the Act` EQUALS `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under the Act` EQUALS `section 9 does not shield the benefit from the claim`
#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `a garnishment for the purposes of the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act` EQUALS `the benefit is garnishable moneys`
#ASSERT `how the benefit stands against the claim` `any other claim` EQUALS `the text does not say`

§ `Act s 10.1 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Act s 14 -- tests`

-- The first anniversary of an assent on 15 January 2024 is 15 January 2025.
#ASSERT `the latest day on which the Act could be brought into force` (YMD 2024 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 1 15
#ASSERT `the day fixed for commencement is within the time section 14 allows` (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 15)
#ASSERT `the day fixed for commencement is within the time section 14 allows` (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2024 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the day fixed for commencement is within the time section 14 allows` (YMD 2024 1 15) (YMD 2025 1 16)
-- An assent on 29 February 2024: the anniversary in 2025 is 28 February (the month arithmetic clamps).
#ASSERT `the latest day on which the Act could be brought into force` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT NOT `the day fixed for commencement is within the time section 14 allows` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2025 3 1)
